  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Skeletal Keypoint Extraction & Deep Learning Pipeline for DVT Risk Assessment\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements a non-invasive, vision-based diagnostic framework that extracts high-fidelity skeletal keypoints from video sequences, performs spatio-temporal feature engineering to quantify mobility indicators, and applies Deep Learning (Bi-Directional LSTMs) and Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs) to assess Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT) risk."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Pipeline Architecture Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "```text\n",
    "                   +-----------------------+\n",
    "                   | Raw Video Stream      |\n",
    "                   +-----------------------+\n",
    "                               |\n",
    "       [Stage 1: Spatial-Temporal Feature Extraction]\n",
    "                               |
    "                               v
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "| 1. Video Integrity Validation (CV2 Integrity Checks)        |\n",
    "| 2. Skeletal Keypoint Localization (MediaPipe Pose 3D)       |\n",
    "| 3. Angular Geometry Computation (Knee & Ankle Angles)       |\n",
    "| 4. Temporal Smoothing & Signal Filtering (Convolutions)     |\n",
    "| 5. Motion Feature Engineering (Immobility & Calf Idle)      |\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "                               |\n",
    "                 | [Structured .npy Sequences]\n",
    "                               v\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "| Stage 2: Modeling & Augmentation                            |\n",
    "|                                                             |\n",
    "| +--------------------------+   +--------------------------+ |\n",
    "| | Bi-Directional LSTM      |   | StyleGAN2-ADA            | |\n",
    "| | Sequence Classifier      |   | Generative Pipeline      | |\n",
    "| | - Packed Sequences       |   | - Latent Space Proj.     | |\n",
    "| | - Attention Output       |   | - Synthetic Expansion    | |\n",
    "| +--------------------------+   +--------------------------+ |\n",
    "|               |                              |              |\n",
    "|               v                              v              |\n",
    "| +--------------------------+   +--------------------------+ |\n",
    "| | Multi-Metric Evaluation  |   | Enhanced Downstream      | |\n",
    "| | (ROC, Confusion Matrix)  |   | Classifier (ResNet)      | |\n",
    "| +--------------------------+   +--------------------------+ |\n",
    "+-------------------------------------------------------------+\n",
    "```"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Component Deep Dive\n",
    "\n",
    "### 1. Robust Video Validation & Preprocessing\n",
    "\n",
    "To prevent downstream failures caused by corrupted, short, or zero-byte recordings, the pipeline incorporates an automated validation gate utilizing OpenCV:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Size Checking:** Discards files falling below a minimum size threshold.\n",
    "- **Header and Codec Validation:** Ensures the system can successfully read the video metadata and retrieve key markers like frame count and FPS."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Pose Landmark Processing (MediaPipe)\n",
    "\n",
    "Using Google's MediaPipe Pose library, the pipeline extracts a 33-landmark 3D skeletal topology from individual frames:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Landmark Tracking:** Focuses specifically on the lower body landmarks: Hip, Knee, Ankle, and Foot (landmarks 23, 25, 27, 31 for Left; 24, 26, 28, 32 for Right).\n",
    "- **Missing Frame Handling:** Automatically handles occlusion or tracking dropouts by mapping missing frames to null vectors (`[0] * 66`) to maintain sequence integrity."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Spatial Angle Geometry Calculations\n",
    "\n",
    "To capture physiological characteristics of posture and activity, Euclidean joint angles are calculated dynamically across consecutive frames using the cosine rule:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\theta = \\arccos\\left( \\frac{\\vec{BA} \\cdot \\vec{BC}}{\\lVert \\vec{BA} \\rVert \\, \\lVert \\vec{BC} \\rVert} \\right)\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Knee Angle:** Computed using Hip-Knee-Ankle landmarks.\n",
    "- **Ankle Angle:** Computed using Knee-Ankle-Foot landmarks."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Dynamic Signal Smoothing\n",
    "\n",
    "Physical noise from tracking jitter is resolved by passing the spatial angular streams through a moving-average convolution filter:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "S_t = \\frac{1}{k} \\sum_{i=0}^{k-1} X_{t-i}\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\n",
    "This maintains spatial boundaries while smoothing out anomalous high-frequency noise."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. DVT Risk Feature Engineering\n",
    "\n",
    "To translate motion dynamics into clinically relevant parameters, three primary indicators are computed across the temporal dimension:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Immobility Ratio:** Calculates the percentage of frames where joint angular velocity (first-order difference) drops below $50\\%$ of the sequence's $75^{\\text{th}}$ percentile.\n",
    "- **Calf Idle Ratio:** Measures the lack of ankle pump activation, which directly corresponds to poor blood circulation.\n",
    "- **Maximum Idle Stretch:** Determines the longest contiguous block of frames without movement, which is converted to seconds using the video frame rate (FPS).\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\n",
    "\\text{Risk Score} = \\frac{\\text{Immobility Ratio} + \\text{Calf Idle Ratio} + \\min\\left(\\dfrac{\\text{Max Idle Stretch}}{\\text{Scaling Factor}},\\, 1.0\\right)}{3}\n",
    "$$"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Bidirectional LSTM Modeling\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of treating clips as isolated frames, the model maps temporal dependencies across frames using an LSTM network:\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Padded and Packed Sequences:** Adjusts input signals to a uniform timeline while using `pack_padded_sequence` to ignore padded zero-frames during backpropagation.\n",
    "- **Bidirectionality:** Captures motion dynamics by analyzing sequences in both forward and backward directions."
   ]
  }
 ],
